  "name": "Kamex Mega Battle",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Kamex Mega Battle (Blastoise Mega Battle) was Japan's second Best in Japan series. Its regional tournaments ran from 19 July to 23 August 1998 in Yokohama, Nagoya, Fukuoka, Sapporo and Kyoto, and the top three of each of the 14 junior and senior sessions won No. 1, No. 2 or No. 3 Trainer trophy cards in acrylic cases, 14 of each, with an invitation to a qualifying league in Tokyo on 30 August 1998. Its winners went on to the Best in Japan final later that day, shown on TV Tokyo's 64 Mario Stadium. The cards were the third and last printing of Mitsuhiro Arita's art of Pikachu holding a trophy.\n\nComputer Search was banned at these tournaments: every player was given a matte Computer Error and had to add it to their deck, playing 61 cards instead of 60. From the size of the tournaments, Pokumon estimates about 896 were handed out.\n\nThe name came back for Kamex Mega Battle 2016, Japan's spring championship that year, which has its own entry.",
